  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The findings are based on a small qualitative sample of ten interviews across four specific, long-established festivals in a single country.",
      "what": "This study analyzes women's labor and gender distribution across curatorial, administrative, and operational roles in four long-running Turkish film festivals. The researchers reviewed 133 festival catalogs and conducted 10 in-person and online interviews with female festival managers and employees to trace historical changes in participation.",
      "why": "It documents how gender disparities in the broader Turkish film industry are replicated within festival organizations, revealing that while women have increasingly managed film funds over the last decade, their roles in most festivals remain restricted to operational tasks rather than leadership or decision-making positions."
    }
